As is well known in the art, in order to be able to map one parameter to another, a correlation must exist between the parameters. The applicants have found that a correlation between the AC component of a PPG signal and blood pressure can be found, but this correlation is highly dependent upon the force applied to the user's skin by the PPG sensor (applicants' FIG. 3). For example, if a force of about 8 Newtons is applied, there is no correlation between blood volume pulse information and blood pressure. If a force of about 2 Newtons is applied, a strong negative correlation existsSVG
